lican incumbent Cory Mills lost renomination to Ryan Elijah, a first-time nominee who has already shifted positions on the 2020 election and drawn local law-enforcement endorsements. The district leans Republican by about five points, but the 2026 environment favors Democrats, and most rating outlets moved the race in their direction. Ratings split between Lean R and Likely R, with two outlets calling it a Tossup and one calling it a Democratic flip.\n\nDemocrat Bale Dalton has out-raised Elijah roughly four to one, holds a cash advantage, and has attracted about $700,000 in outside support, while prediction markets still give Democrats only about a one-in-three chance. With essentially no recent public polling of the matchup, the race sits just on the Republican side of even, with wide uncertainty typical of a low-information open seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4211, "margin": -1.21}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4651, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3497, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3248, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2949, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3493, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3328, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3464, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3386, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3794, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3754, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3743, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4206, "margin": -1.8}]}